# R session state - machine-local, never useful to anyone else
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rapp.history

# RStudio
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# Knitr / R Markdown build artefacts
*_files/
*_cache/
*.utf8.md
*.knit.md

# Compiled Stan models. bridgestan writes a shared library next to each .stan
# file; those are large, platform specific, and rebuilt from the cached source
# in a couple of minutes. The .stan and .json alongside them come from
# posteriordb and are re-fetched just as easily.
stan_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*

# The mid-run checkpoint. Written every 3 models so a crash does not cost the
# whole sweep, and of no use once the run finishes - it is a strictly smaller
# copy of benchmark_results.rds. It used to be tracked, and having a plausible
# looking half-finished results file sitting in the repo is what made it
# possible for analyze_results.R to read it by mistake for six models instead
# of seven.
benchmark_results_partial.rds

# Note on the other .rds files: benchmark_config.rds, benchmark_results.rds and
# posteriordb_discovery.rds ARE tracked on purpose. They are the saved output of
# a benchmark run that takes network access and real time to reproduce, so they
# stay in the repo as the evidence behind the figures and summary tables.
